research/audit/wave5-topology-function-spaces.provenance.jsonl:33:{"id": "ex-dini-on-the-unit-interval", "statement": "ai-altered", "proof": "ai-generated", "evidence": "semantic-source", "urls": ["https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dini%27s_theorem", "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uniform_limit_theorem"], "rationale": "A worked instance of the sourced Dini theorem on [0,1] together with its standard sharpness discussion. The clipped identities s_k(t) = min{t, 1 - a_k} form a nondecreasing sequence of continuous functions converging pointwise to the continuous identity, which is a routine instance rather than a novel construction, and the failure clause reuses this page's ramps to show that continuity of the limit cannot be dropped, which is the standard remark accompanying Dini's theorem. Specialisation of a sourced theorem plus a standard sharpness witness, hence ai-altered. Local verification; note that the positive half is also proved directly by the bound |s_k(t) - t| <= a_k, independent of Dini.", "alpha_concurred": false, "at": "2026-08-05"}
